course: dictionary
lesson: 7809
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word quest is a good example. «a quest for the lost treasure» is a long search or journey to find something important. «the quest for a cure» means a strong effort to achieve something.
explain: In games, a quest is a mission or task the player must complete, as in «a side quest». To choose the right meaning, read the words around quest. Are there treasure, heroes or journeys? Or are there players and levels? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Quest can also be a verb, but it is literary, so you will mostly meet it in old stories and poems. To quest means to search for something. In a legend, a knight who quests is out searching for something important.
fact: A quest is a long search or journey to find or get something important.
fact: «the quest for» means a strong effort to achieve something, such as «the quest for a cure».
fact: In games, a quest is a mission or task the player must complete, such as «a side quest».
fact: In myths and legends, heroes go on quests, like King Arthur's knights searching for the Holy Grail.
fact: As a verb (literary), quest means to search for something.
exercise: «The knights set out on a quest for the Holy Grail.» What does quest mean here? | A type of armour | *A long search for something important | A boat race on the river | A quiet rest at an inn
exercise: Ellie says, «I'm on a quest to finish this level.» Which meaning fits? | A long walk to the shops | *A mission the player must complete | A strong dislike of games | A map of the town
exercise: «The scientists are on a quest for answers.» What does this mean? | A fast race to the finish | *A strong effort to find something | A party with lots of food | A short sleep
test: «She went on a quest to find her lost cat.» Which word means the same as quest here? | A broken toy | A nap | *A search | A dinner party
test: Max reads, «The old poem says the hero will quest through the dark forest.» What does quest mean as a verb? | To cook | To sleep | *To search | To laugh
exam: In which sentence does quest mean a mission in a game? | *Finish the side quest to unlock the castle. | Her quest for the lost treasure began at dawn. | The scientists began a quest for a cure. | They went on a quest over the hills.
